window.SUSAN_VERB_CARDS = [{"number":1,"word":"annoy","text":"Hello dear darling, this is “annoy”. En~hey, go away, don’t annoy me, fly!\nEn~ok, let’s look at the word--“annoy”. \nThis is a fly, and the fly is annoying the lion. \nOh no, there’re 2 flies, one, two, the two flies are annoying the lion, and the lion is really annoyed.\n “Go away, go away, don’t annoy me!”\nFlies are so annoying. \n此处强调发音n遍. 再举个例子：you are annoying me.\n（phonics part）“oy” for \\ɔɪ\\   \\ə-n-ɔɪ\\\nWhat’s annoying? 啊~~ flies and mosquitos. En~go away.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-099.jpg"},{"number":2,"word":"approach","text":"Hello dear darling, what’s this? This is new verb, it’s called-- approach \n(发音重复n次，顺势举例) I am approaching you.\nNow look at the picture, what’s this? Oh, it’s an alligator. What‘s this? It’s a hippo. \nThe alligator is approaching the hippo, and the hippo is approaching the alligator.\nSo, the animals are approaching each other very carefully.\nNow look, everyone, what is approaching me? It’s a duck. A cute duck is approaching me.\nWhat about now? (乖巧脸) It’s a rabbit, a rabbit is approaching me. Squeak squeak~~~\n(roar~~roar~~~) A tiger is approaching me, I need to run away~\nOh no! A car is approaching me, bye~~~","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-100.jpg"},{"number":3,"word":"attack","text":"Hello dear darling, what’s this? This is a verb, it’s called --attack. What does it mean?\nI see 2 lions, and this lion is so angry that he wants to attack(顺手比划+重复发音)\nOk, ‘ck’ makes \\k\\ sound, so \\ə-tæ-k\\\nThis lion is really angry, and is attacking another lion’s head, and this lion(委屈脸) is saying ‘oh no, don’t attack me, oh no’\nLook at this, oh this is a lion, and I think this lion gets angry, roar~~~and this lion is attaching an elephant. Oh no, who’s gonna win? I don’t know.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-097.jpg"},{"number":4,"word":"bite","text":"Susan, what are you doing? En~ I am biting my finger. No, no, no, don’t bite your finger, it’s bad.\nBite, bite, (phonics part) I blabla E, makes \\ai\\. ‘\\b-aɪ-t\\’\nThis is a leopard, and the leopard is biting the crocodile’s tail.\nOuch! Don’t bite me so painful.\nAnd I know a very funny poem with ‘bite’ in it, now let’s listen to it, it goes like this: \nOne, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive.\nSix, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. \nWhy did you let it go? Cause it bit my fingers so.  \nWhich finger did it bite?  This little finger on the right. Ouch~~","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-098.jpg"},{"number":5,"word":"break","text":"B-R-E-A-K~~\nLook, this turtle is breaking out of its shell. \n‘br’ makes \\br\\ sound, （憋了很久的br终于发出了break的音，这便是Susan吸引小盆友之道）\nThis strong little turtle is breaking out of its shell, the egg is broken into pieces.\nLet’s look at this one, it’s a watch. Can I break my watch? Bang, bang, bang….\nNo, no, no, don’t break your watch, your watch will be broken.\nWhat about your glasses? Bang! Ouch, your glasses will be broken, don’t break them.\nHow about your heart? Oh, I am so sad if you break my heart.\nDon’t break my heart, mommy. I don’t wanna do homework.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-095.jpg"},{"number":6,"word":"brush","text":"Susan, what are you doing? I’m brushing my teeth. Up and down, in and out, 啊~~~~\n‘sh’ makes ‘\\ʃ\\’ sound,  \\ brʌʃ\\\nLook at the elephant, the elephant is brushing its body. \nThis is so funny, we don’t brush our body, we brush our teeth, right?\nSo, mommy? What are you doing? I’m brushing my teeth.\nDaddy? What are you doing? (粗声大气) I’m brushing my teeth.\nOh, baby, are you brushing your teeth? En~yee~, but I don’t want to.\nI don’t like brushing my teeth, but I must.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-096.jpg"},{"number":7,"word":"build","text":"Hello dear darling, what’s this? Oh, this card says, ‘build’ x N.\n‘b’ says \\b\\, ‘b-il-d’.\nOh, this is a squirrel, and the squirrel looks so happy, why? Because the squirrel is building a snowman.\nOh, I love snowman, I wanna build a snowman too, but, Ah~oh, it’s summer now, there’s no snow, but I wanna build a snowman.\nOr maybe, I can build with the building blocks. One, two, building, building. \nLook! I am building a building. Look this, wo~it’s gonna be so tall.\nOne more, oh two more, now look at my building, it’s so cool, right?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-093.jpg"},{"number":8,"word":"carry","text":"Susan, what are you doing? Susan is carrying something. \nWhat am I carrying? Ta~da, I’m carrying ‘carry’. Wo~carry x N遍发音.\nThe ending ‘y’ makes the \\i\\ sound. So ‘k-æ-ri’, ‘k-æ-ri’…..\nWhat’s this? This is a beaver, the beaver has two big teeth. Oh, the beaver is happily carrying a log. \nSo now, can you guess what Susan is carrying? Dada~Susan is carrying candy, so sweet.\nWhat about now? Meow, meow, yes, Susan is carrying a cat.\nWhat’s Susan carrying? Oh, Susan is carrying a baby.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-094.jpg"},{"number":9,"word":"catch","text":"Everybody, look, this is a new word called ‘catch’\n‘ch’ makes \\tʃ\\, \\k-æ-tʃ\\\nWhat is the baby crocodile catching? The baby crocodile is catching a poor fish.\nWhat about monkey? A monkey can catch bananas. X 2\nWhat about a tiger? Roar, a tiger can catch a sheep. X2\nWhat about mommy? Who can mommy catch? My mommy can catch me.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-091.jpg"},{"number":10,"word":"charge 冲","text":"Susan, what are you doing? I’m, I‘m charging.\nOk, look at this, the hippo is charging too.\n‘ch’ makes (引诱小盆友回答) \\tʃ\\, good job！‘ch’ makes \\tʃ\\, ‘\\tʃ-ɑː-dʒ\\’\nCharge means you start to run really fast to attack.\nNow look at the hippo, the hippo is charging at its enemy.\nNow, moo, here comes a bull, the bull is charging. Then the horse is charging. (各种拟声)\nWhat about the elephant? Trumpet, the elephant is charging.\nLion! Roar! This lion is charging. Run away, so scary.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-092.jpg"},{"number":11,"word":"chase","text":"Hey, fly, don’t go away! Susan, what’re you doing? I am chasing, I am chasing that fly.\nThe little dinosaur is chasing the fly too.\n‘ch’ again（引诱小盆友回答) , yes, ‘ch’ makes \\tʃ\\, \\tʃeɪs\\\nThe dinosaur is chasing the fly.\nRoar! look the tiger, what is the tiger chasing? Trumpet, elephant.\nThe elephant is chasing somebody too. Oh, no, the horse is chasing somebody too.\nThe bull is chasing somebody too. What? A bull is chasing the chick? \nOh, the chick’s chasing somebody. Oh, no, the chick is chasing me. \nWhat a crazy zoo!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-089.jpg"},{"number":12,"word":"clean","text":"Hey, Susan, what are you doing? I’m cleaning the lens, I think it’s a little dirty, do you think so?\nOk, this word is ‘clean’. When you see something dirty, you clean it.\nNow look at the squirrels, the squirrels are cleaning their home.\nDid you clean you home? Yes, I cleaned my home today.\nNow look at this, this is a dirty window. Oh, no it’s so dirty, I must clean it. Now look at the window, it’s so clean.\nNow look at the door, the door is so dirty, let’s clean it. Now, it’s so clean.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-090.jpg"},{"number":13,"word":"climb","text":"Hi, Susan, what are you doing? I am climbing a tree.\n‘cl’ makes \\kl\\ sound.\nLook at this, this is a raccoon. The raccoon is climbing a tree to escape. Why? Because something is chasing it.\nWhat’s this? It’s a monkey. Can monkey climb a tree? Yes, a monkey can climb a tree. Very good.\nWhat about panda? A panda can climb a tree even thought it’s a little fat. A panda can climb a tree.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-087.jpg"},{"number":14,"word":"compare","text":"Hey everybody, what is Susan doing? Susan is comparing. compare x2.\nThese two hippos are comparing their open mouth, and I’m joining them (啊~) and comparing too.\nNow, let’s compare the owl and the cow, which one is bigger? Is the cow bigger, or is the owl bigger? Yes, the cow is bigger.\nNow let’s compare the car and the bus, which one is faster? (各种演) A car is faster.\nAnd now let’s compare your mommy and daddy, let’s compare who is taller. Is your mommy taller, or your daddy taller?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-088.jpg"},{"number":15,"word":"cook","text":"Hello dear darling, today we’re gonna look at another verb called ‘cook’. Cook x2\n‘oo’ makes \\u\\ sound, that’s right. ‘k-u-k’.\nLook at the monkey, the monkey is cooking meat under the sun. \nUsually, we cook over the fire, Susan can cook very well(给自己一个大大赞). \nI like cooking. Does your mommy like cooking too?\nNow look at this, potato, can we cook potatoes? Yes, yes, so yummy.\nCan we cook tomatoes? En, tomatoes are so yummy.\nCan we cook eggs? Of course, eggs are so yummy.\nCan we cook flowers? Ew…","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-085.jpg"},{"number":16,"word":"cover","text":"Hello dear darling, what is this? This is a new word called ‘cover’. Cover x3\n‘er’ makes \\ər\\ sound, ‘\\kʌvər\\’.\nLook at this, this is a lion, the lion is covering its dinner. En, looks like yummy meat. The lion is covering its dinner.\nShush, what happened? The baby is sleeping. Oh, no, the baby has nothing to cover it, come on, give me something.\nA hat? No, a hat is too small to cover the baby. \nA t-shirt, maybe, let’s cover the baby with the t-shirt. No, i think we need a blanket, cover the baby.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-086.jpg"},{"number":17,"word":"dance","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is dancing. Dance x N\n‘ce’ makes \\s\\ sound, (假装听小朋友的回答) yes, that’s right. ‘d-æ-n-s’\nOh, the panda is dancing. Can you dance? Yes, let’s dance!\nOh, the grandmas are dancing, so many grandmas are dancing. Slowly, and grandmas are dancing fast.\nOh, what about the penguin? The penguin is dancing slowly, and the penguin is dancing fast.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-083.jpg"},{"number":18,"word":"defeat","text":"Susan is so sad, why? Because I was defeated by my baby. Defeat x N\nThis lion is as sad as Susan, because the lion is defeated by the tiger. \n‘d’ makes \\d\\, \\dɪˈfiːt\\\nOk, now let’s look at the horse and the donkey, the horse can run very fast, the donkey can run, but the horse can run faster, so the horse can defeat the donkey.\nWhat about a bus and a car? The car can win, because the car is faster, the car can defeat the bus.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-084.jpg"},{"number":19,"word":"dig","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is digging, dig x N\n‘d’ makes \\d\\, \\d-i-g\\\nI like digging, do you like digging? \nNow look at this picture, this is a badger, this badger is digging a long tunnel.\nWhat else can dig? A rabbit. A rabbit can dig a hole, it’s called a burrow, a rabbit can dig a burrow.\nWhat about the dog? The dog can dig, a dog is digging for a bone.\nEn, can you dig for something?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-081.jpg"},{"number":20,"word":"dive","text":"Splish! Splash! Hey Susan, what are you doing? Susan is diving, dive xn.\nLook at the ‘v’, the ‘v’ makes \\v\\ sound. D-aɪ-v. Diving! Splish! Splash!\nThis is a platypus, the platypus is diving into the water. \nWhen you diving, you can swim with a lot of fish.\nWhat’s this? This’s a penguin, a penguin can not fly, but a penguin can dive into the water.\nCan you dive? Do you want to try? Let’s dive! Splish! Splash!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-082.jpg"},{"number":21,"word":"drink","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is drinking. Susan is drinking juice. Drink, juice.\n‘dr’ makes \\dr\\, dr-ɪŋ-k.\nLook at the picture, there’s a tiger, the tiger is drinking water. En, the water is so good. But I think the juice is better. Can you guess what is Susan drinking now? Is it water? No. \nWhat kind of juice? Apple juice? No, Susan is drinking pear and grape juice.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-079.jpg"},{"number":22,"word":"escape","text":"Susan what are you doing? Susan’s escaping, because something scary is after me, I’m escaping.\n‘A’ blabla ‘e’ makes\\ei\\ sound,  \\ɪˈskeɪp\\\nLook at the mice, the mice are escaping the big wave, \nSomething is after me. It’s a dog, a dog is coming toward me, I’m so afraid, escape! Escape! The dog is coming.\nOh no, the bull is coming, escape! Escape!\nRoar! A tiger is coming, escape! Escape!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-080.jpg"},{"number":23,"word":"fart","text":"Ew! What’s so smelly? Someone must have farted!\nOh, it’s so smelly, look at this, this is a skunk, the skunk is farting to warn off the enemy. Go away enemy! 噗~~\n“oh, I must to run.” So the enemy runs away.\nYou know another way of saying fart is ‘toot’. A baby can toot, and mommy can toot, and daddy’s toot can be really loud.\nAnd some toots are long, some toots are short. Do you fart?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-077.jpg"},{"number":24,"word":"feed","text":"Good baby, one more! What am I doing? I am feeding my baby. \\f-ei-d\\\nFeed means, I will you some food to eat.\nNow look at the penguin, this is mommy penguin, and mommy penguin is feeding this little penguin. The mother penguin is feeding its baby fish, because a baby penguin likes to eat fish. Now mommy penguin is feeding the baby penguin.\nWhat does your mom feed you? Food, pizza, pasta, everything, right?\nHow about a rabbit? What do you feed a rabbit? Carrot!\nWhat about a ‘moo’ cow? You feed the cow grass.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-078.jpg"},{"number":25,"word":"feel","text":"Ok, Susan what are you doing? I am feeling happy!  \\f-i:-d\\\nNow look at the lion, is the lion feeling happy? No, this lion is feeling angry!\nCan you guess how I am feeling now? Yes, I’m feeling bored, yes, I am feeling bored.\nHow am I feeling? I am feeling sleepy. Sleepy.\nAnd then, how am I feeling? I think I am feeling hungry? \nDo you have anything for me to eat? \nAnd I’m feeling so sad.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-075.jpg"},{"number":26,"word":"fight","text":"“grandma, why didn’t you wake me up?”\n“what? you promised wake me up! not my fault!”\nhey, grandma, grandpa, what are you doing? why are you fighting?\n“no, we are not fighting, we are only quarrelling ”\nlook, they are fighting. fight xN\nstop fighting! no fighting, fighting is bad!\nif you fight, you’re gonna hurt yourself, you’re gonna hurt you face, hurt you body, fight is not good for anyone.\nlook, the lions are wildly fighting each other. \nstop fighting! let’s say it together to stop them,l ok?\n“stop fighting!” thank you.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-076.jpg"},{"number":27,"word":"float","text":"Hello dear darling, today we’re gonna learn another word called – float.\n‘fl’ makes \\fl\\, \\f-l-oʊ-t\\.\nNow look at the picture, there’s a tiger, and the tiger is floating on the surface.\nFloating is cool, if you want to learn how to swim, you must know how to float, usually I would float like this.\nOk, now look at this one, this is a boat, remember we can row a boat. A boat can stay on top of the water too. A boat can float on the see.\nHere comes an umbrella, can an umbrella float? Yes, look, the umbrella is floating.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-073.jpg"},{"number":28,"word":"fly","text":"Hi everybody, what is Susan doing? Susan is trying to fly, but I can’t fly. Fly x N\nLet’s try to fly higher, fly! I can’t fly.\nHere ‘y’ makes \\ai\\ sound, \\f-l-ai\\\nLook at this, this is a bat, the bat is flying. The bat is flying so happily.\nAnd what else can fly? An owl. An owl can fly too.\nAnd daddy says “hey, I want to fly too”. But I’m sorry daddy, you can’t fly. \n“my daddy cannot fly, but he doesn’t know why. \nA big owl coming, flies on by, and he says nothing but byebye!”","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-074.jpg"},{"number":29,"word":"follow","text":"One, two, three, go! One, two, three! Hey, Susan, what are you doing? Look, I am marching with all my friends by me, because they are following me. Follow x N\n‘ow’ makes \\əʊ\\ sound. \\fɒləʊ\\\nOh, look, this duck is following the robot. \nDo you know who is following me? 1,2,3, go! 1,2,3, go! A cow is following me. \n1,2,3, go! 1,2,3, go! An owl is coming. Follow me! Follow me!\n1,2,3, go! 1,2,3, go! A horse is following. \nOnik! Onik! “wait for me! I want to follow too.”","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-071.jpg"},{"number":30,"word":"gasp","text":"hooray! I just finished 100-meter race, I was the last one, but I’m so tired and happy!\nso, that’s why I am gasping. ok, gasp, gasp.\nlook at them, the lion and tiger are gasping for air after fighting. they fought and they felt so tired, they are gasping.\noh, mommy is feeling so tired. why? mommy? why are you feeling so tired? ‘I’m gasping, because I’ve got so many vegetables.’ \ngrandma, why are you gasping? I just finish dancing, I’m so tired.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-072.jpg"},{"number":31,"word":"give","text":"Hello dear darling, today we’re gonna look at another verb--give.\nWhat does give mean? If you want something, you could say “could you please give me something?”\nNow look at the squirrel, the squirrel is giving a speech. \n‘ok, everybody, today I wanna talk about blabla’. The squirrel is giving a speech.\nAnd sometimes if you want something, you could say “Mommy, could you please give me that cap?” “sure, baby, here you” are, baby, this is your cap.”\n“Mommy, could you please give me the hat?”  “Sure, baby, here you” are, this is your hat.”\n‘Mommy, could you give me the sofa?’ ‘En, baby, I think the sofa is too big.’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-069.jpg"},{"number":32,"word":"grin","text":"Susan, what are you doing? I am grinning.\n‘gr’ makes \\gr\\ sound.\nNow look at the horse, the horse is grinning happily.\nWhen you grin, you willl show your teeth. Do you have white teeth? Do you have beautiful teeth? Show me.\nOh, look, this boy is grinning. How about the pig? The pig is so happy too.\nWhat about grandpa? Grandpa, where are you teeth? “Oh, no, I forgot my denture.”","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-070.jpg"},{"number":33,"word":"growl咆哮","text":"Look at the tiger, what’s the tiger doing? The tiger is growling. \n‘gr’ also makes \\gr\\ sound. \\ɡraʊl\\\nYou sound so scary! Very good growling.\nNow the tiger is growling angrily. Why? Tiger? Why are you growling? “Somebody ate my food, roar!”\nWhat else can growl? A tiger? Of course. And a dog? An angry dog will growl too. I’m so scared.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-067.jpg"},{"number":34,"word":"hang","text":"Hi everyone, do you know what Susan is doing? I’m trying to hang my cap, but it’s too high, I can’t reach. Ok, anyway, I tried.\nI was hanging my cap, finally I got the hanger there.\nNow look at this, this animal is called sloth, a sloth moves very slowly. This is a sloth, and the sloth is lazily hanging from a branch. Hang~ oh, I’m so happy, there.\nWell, it seems that you are so happy, the monkey can also hang happily. A monkey can hang and swing, monkey hang!\n‘oink, oink, I want to try too.’ A piggy wants to hang? That’s not a good idea.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-068.jpg"},{"number":35,"word":"hatch","text":"Hello everyone, I just hatched! No, I’m just joking. This turtle can hatch, I cannot hatch.\n‘ch’ makes \\tʃ\\ sound. \\hætʃ\\\nThe turtle is hatching from its shell. Happy birthday! So the turtle is hatching from its shell.\nWhich other animal can hatch from the egg? Let me see, a chick can hatch from the egg.\nHow about a duck? Yes, a duck can also hatch.\nWhat about a penguin? Yes, a little penguin can hatch from the egg.\nWhat about a baby? No, no, no, a baby is not hatched.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-065.jpg"},{"number":36,"word":"hate","text":"Susan, what are you doing? I’m looking at something I hate.\nHate means you really really don’t like something, I hate it!\nLook at the tow lions, the lions hate each other. The lions are looking at each other angrily, because they hate each other.\nDo you hate something? Oh, you hate vegetables? I hate vegetables! But vegetables are good for you.\nI hate carrots, mommy! I don’t want to eat carrots! Oh, but carrots are really good for you.\nDo you hate candy? No, I love candy!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-066.jpg"},{"number":37,"word":"have","text":"Hello everyone, what am I doing? I am having a hot bath. Have a hot bath, just like the monkey.\nAnd you know what? Have can also mean you own something. For example, I have a nose, I have two eyes, and I have many, many other things. For example, I have juice, and I have a t-shirt, I have a tomato, I have a bus, I have a coconut, I have a baby. I have a baby?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-063.jpg"},{"number":38,"word":"head-butt","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is head-butting with the bull. \n(重复N遍发音) how do you read that? Very good!\nLook at the two monkeys, the monkeys are head-butting each other. Can you head-butt with your mom?\nNow look at these two animals, a bull and a donkey, they’re gonna head-butt. Who do you think can win? Let’s wait and see! Oh, hooray, the bull wins. Head-butt!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-064.jpg"},{"number":39,"word":"hide","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is hiding.\nLook, the squirrel is hiding a nut in a tree. What is the squirrel doing? Hiding! Very good!\nNow, Susan can hide. there’s song that we can sing together, it’s called “where is thumbkin”.\nthumbkin, pointer, tall man, ring man, pinky. \n“Where is thumbkin, where is thumbkin, here I am, here I am.\nHow are you today, sir? very well and thank you, run and hide, run and hide.”","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-061.jpg"},{"number":40,"word":"hoard \\hɔːrd\\ 囤积","text":"hello dear darling, look at the rabbit, the rabbit is so happy. why? because the rabbit is hoarding so many carrots.\nhoarding means you put many, many things that you want together, as many as possible.\nsusan wants to hoard many, many things. I want to hoard oranges as many as possible.\nI want to hoard sunglasses, 1, 2, 3, 4, so many pairs.\nI want to hoard caps, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, so many caps.\nI want to hoard watches, one is not enough, many, many ...\nand I want to hoard so many cards, I am so happy.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-062.jpg"},{"number":41,"word":"hop","text":"‘Handy spandy, Jack-a-dandy, loves plum-cake and sugar-candy. He brought some at a grocery shop, and out he came, hop hop hop. ’\n‘p’ says \\p\\\nNow look at this, what’s this? Very good, it’s a rabbit. What’s the rabbit doing? Very good! The rabbit is hopping. The rabbit is hopping through the grass. \nGreen grass, I love it, why no walk through the grass. Swish-swash, swish-swash, I want to hop. Hop through the grass.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-059.jpg"},{"number":42,"word":"hug","text":"‘hush little baby, don’t say a word, mom’s gonna buy you a mockingbird, if that mockingbird won’t sing, mom’s gonna buy you a diamond ring’\nHi everyone, what is susan doing? Susan is hugging the baby, and susan is singing a lullaby.\nLook, the father monkey is hugging its baby with love. All the babies love to say ‘huggy, huggy’. Now comes this baby who says ‘daddy, daddy, huggy, huggy. ‘\n‘ok’ ‘hey dad, don’t’ hug me up side down.’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-060.jpg"},{"number":43,"word":"jump","text":"hello everyone, Susan is jumping so happily. I love jumping, jump xN.\n‘j’ makes \\dʒ\\\nnow look at the monkey, the monkey is jumping up and down, jump up and down.\ncan you jump? maybe you can, maybe you can’t, but jumping is really fun.\nhere comes grandma, grandma says ‘I can jump!’ good job, grandma!\nhere comes mom, ‘I can jump higher!’ good job, mommy!\nhere comes the baby, ‘hey! I can jump highest!’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-057.jpg"},{"number":44,"word":"kick","text":"Splish-splash! What happened? Look, the mole is kicking its enemy into the water. Look how happy he is, he is kicking its enemy into the water.\n‘ck’ makes \\k\\, how do you read this? Good job!\nNow tell me, can you kick a cat? No, don’t kick the cat, stroke the cat.\nDon’t kick the dog, no, no, no, you stroke the dog.\nWhat can you kick then? A football! You can kick a football. Oh, this is too big for my finger man.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-058.jpg"},{"number":45,"word":"lead","text":"Hello everyone, today we’re gonna look at another verb called ‘lead’.\n’ea’ makes \\i:\\ sound\nLook, i see three zebras, this zebra saying ‘i lead!’ The others are following. \nThis zebra is leading, the other zebras are following.\nNow look at this, grandpa is leading and grandma is following. \nAnd, daddy is leading and mommy is following. \nAnd now the monkey is leading and then the panda is following, and panda says ‘wait for me, you are too fast’.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-055.jpg"},{"number":46,"word":"lean","text":"I’m so comfortable. Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is leaning against a tree.\nNow look at this, this is the tree, and this is the badger, the badger is leaning against\nthe tree. So comfortable!\nWhat else can you lean on? Maybe my shoulder?\nSo let’s see, here comes a rabbit, hop, hop. The rabbit is leaning on me, that’s cool.\nHere comes a panda, ok, here, come, come. All right, the panda is leaning on me too.\nAnd then, here comes a deer, the deer is leaning on me, I start to feel a little heavy. \nHere comes a pig, the pig is leaning on me. \nThen, trumpet, what? An elephant is leaning on me. Too heavy!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-056.jpg"},{"number":47,"word":"leave","text":"Oh, Susan, why are you crying? Well, the squirrel is sadly leaving its home. It’s leaving home, so the squirrel is feeling so sad.\nI don’t want to leave home, so I’m a little blue today, I’m not happy.\nSusan, susan, can you play with me? Sorry, leave me alone, I’m so sad.\nOink, oink, susan, can you play with me? Sorry, leave me alone, I’m a little sad today.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-053.jpg"},{"number":48,"word":"lick","text":"So yummy! Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is licking my finger.\n‘ck’ makes \\k\\\nNow look at this two animals, they are badgers, this badger is licking its friend to show affection. (表达爱意)\nBadgers are funny, you lick to show affection. \nBaby, let me lick you. Ew, mommy don’t do that! You say ‘mommy don’t lick me!’ \nWhile we can lick something else. Grape jam! Yummy, yum. Watermelon juice, sweet. \nmarmalade(橘子酱), yummy, yum.\nHamburger, yummy, I love cheese. Noodles, oh, hot, hot!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-054.jpg"},{"number":49,"word":"listen","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is listening to music.\nNow look at the monkey, this monkey is peacefully listening to music. I like listening to music, do you like listening to music?\nNow listen, what can you hear? I think I hear a mosquito. \nListen! What’s this? Oh, it’s a tiger.\nOh, it’s raining. Pitter-patter, pitter-patter. ‘rain rain go away, come back here another day’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-051.jpg"},{"number":50,"word":"look","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is looking at herself in the mirror.\nLook at the rabbit, the rabbit is looking at itself in the mirror.\n‘oo’ says \\ ʊ\\\nYou have two eyes, and eyes can help you look. \nlook at this, what’s this? I see a hammer.\nLoot at this! I see a key. Loot at this! I see a jacket. \nNow everyone, look up! Look down! Look to the right! Look to the left! Look around! Look at you finger!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-052.jpg"},{"number":51,"word":"measure","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is measuring her hair. \nLook at these two leopards, what are they doing? They are measuring their height(\\ai\\). This leopard is standing here and say ‘how tall it is?’\nWhat else can we measure? We can measure the bed, this is a very long bed. \nCan we measure the building? The building is so high, I don’t think I can measure it.\nWhy don’t we measure our finger? Pretty long, right?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-049.jpg"},{"number":52,"word":"move(移动之外还有‘动’的意思)","text":"Hello everybody, what is Susan doing? Susan is moving her eyes. \nCan you move your eyes? show me, that’s right.\nCan you move your ears? good. \nCan you move your eyebrows? Up and down, up and down.\nCan you move your mouth? that’s right, so funny.\nCan you move your shoulder? \nLook at the squirrel, the squirrels are moving to a new home. \nSpeaking of that, I need to move my home.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-050.jpg"},{"number":53,"word":"observe","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is observing. I am observing the balloon.\nThis is a new verb, it means to look carefully.\n‘er’ makes \\er\\ sound. How do you read this? Yes, observe!\nNow look at the elephant, what is the elephant doing? The elephant is looking at something very carefully. The elephant is observing.\nLet’s observe the balloon, it’s pink, and it’s so round.\nLet’s observe the candle, this candle is pink too, and it’s so small.\nThe elephant is observing something with a magnifying glass.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-047.jpg"},{"number":54,"word":"overeat","text":"Hello everyone, Susan is eating, and I think I may have overeaten. I had too much food. \nLook at this bear, this bear has super big belly, why? Because this bear often overeats. \nAnd overeat means you eat too much.\nLook at this piggy, the piggy is so fat, why? Because the piggy is always overeating. \nDaddy, daddy, stop eating. You are too fat, you have overeating too much food. Don’t overeat!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-048.jpg"},{"number":55,"word":"pee","text":"What’s that sound? Someone must be pee.yes, it’s the hippo, the hippo is peeing.\nHippo, don’t pee on the grass. Look, he’s peeing on the grass.\nLet’s say together ‘don’t pee on the grass’! Very good.\nHere comes a dog, the dog wants to pee too. Can the dog pee on the sofa? No no no, let’s tell the dog, don’t do it, ‘don’t pee on the sofa! ‘good job!\nWhat about on the desk? No, no , ‘don’t pee on the desk! ‘\nWhat about in the van.? No, no.\nCan the dog pee on the moon? No, you can’t go to the moon.\nI think I wanna go pee, byebye.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-045.jpg"},{"number":56,"word":"play","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is playing, Susan is playing the Rubik’s Cube. It’s got so many colors, I like to play it. And look at the hippos, the hippos are playing on the seesaw, up down, up down. \n‘pl’ makes \\pl\\ sound.\nLook, they are playing happily, do you like to play? Of course! All children like to play, everybody likes to play. \nWhat do you like to play? I like to play a balloon.  And I like to play the ball.  And I like to play with mommy best.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-046.jpg"},{"number":57,"word":"poke \\pəʊk\\ 探，戳","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is poking the balloon. This is so much fun!\nNow look at the cat, this big cat is poking around inside the hole. \n‘o’ blabla ‘e’ here is red as\\oʊ\\\nYou can poke Susan on my face. Where else you can poke? Maybe you can try poking on a cake. That’s funny.\nAnd sometime you can poke through the paper. You can not poke through the card.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-043.jpg"},{"number":58,"word":"poop","text":"Ew, why is it so smelly? It’s you, hippo! Look, the hippo is pooping on the grass, that’s why so smelly. The hippo is pooping on the grass, so smelly.\nHippo, you can not poop on the grass, the grass will be dirty. \nHere comes the naughty dog again, don’t tell me you wanna poop.\nOh dear, hey dog, where are you going? Don’t go in the car, you cannot poop on the car.\nTell him, tell him to stop! Hey stop dog! Don’t poop on the bed.\nYou wanna poop on the sun? No, you can’t go there.\nWhere should the dog go pooping? In the toilet.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-044.jpg"},{"number":59,"word":"pounce \\paʊns\\ 猛扑，突袭","text":"Hello everyone, what does Susan do? Susan pounces on you! So scary!\nLook at this, what‘s the leopard doing? The leopard is pouncing on its prey(猎物). The leopard can pounce so high. \nWhich other animal can pounce? A cat can pounce, a cat can pounce onto a mouse.\nWhat’s this, it’s a lion, a lion can pounce on its prey too. And a tiger can pounce.\nHere’s your daddy, do you wanna pounce on him? Let’s pounce!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-041.jpg"},{"number":60,"word":"pout \\paʊt\\ 撅嘴","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is pouting. \nWhy am I pouting? Because my mom says I cannot eat candy. And I am mad, I’m not happy, so I’m pouting.\nNow let’s pout together, it’s funny, isn’t it? But don’t pout too much, because when your mom says something, she means something good for you.\nFor example, your mom may say “hey don’t watch too much TV” ‘But I wanna watch TV’\nDo you know why canrnot watch TV? Because it’s too bad for you eyes, you cannot keep watching for too long. \nAnd you mom will say ’hey, don’t eat too much ice-cream’ ‘but I wanna eat ice-cream’. Well, but it’s too cold for you, you cannot eat too much.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-042.jpg"},{"number":61,"word":"pretend (pretend to do, pretend cake)","text":"hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is pretending to blow a bubble. Look at this one, this word is called ‘pretend’. \n‘pr’ makes the \\pr\\ sound.\nWhat does ‘pretend’ mean? Pretending means you are imaging as it is true.\nFor example, I can pretend to be a cat, I’m not a cat, but I’m only pretending.\nHow about let’s make a pretend cake? Woo, it’s a really, really yummy cake.\nNow Susan is pretending to be eating it. Now Susan is pretending to be sleeping, because I’m so sleepy, bye.\nThe hippo is pretending to be a rhino.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-039.jpg"},{"number":62,"word":"protect","text":"Hello dear darling, today we’re gonna look at another word called protect.\nLook at this snake, what is the snake doing? The snake is covering its own eggs with the leaves. Why? Because this mommy snake wants to protect these eggs with leaves. Cover them and no one can see them. This is what a mommy does.\nNow look at this one, here comes a little chicken, this little chick is so cute, and who can protect the chick? It’s the mommy, a hen can protect the chicks. \nWhat about the baby? Who can protect the baby? Of course, it’s your mom and dad.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-040.jpg"},{"number":63,"word":"puke","text":"Hi everyone, Susan is feeling bad, because I wanna puke. Oh my god, I’m so sorry. \nLook at this one, this is a platypus, and this platypus is puking.\nPoor platypus! The platypus wants to puke, why? Look at this, I think I see some bad fish. I know why the platypus is puking, because the platypus ate some bad fish.\nOh my god, the dog is puking too, why? Maybe because the dog ate some bad dog food.\nThe baby is puking, because the baby drank(drink?) too much milk.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-037.jpg"},{"number":64,"word":"pull","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is pulling her hair. Ouch! Don’t pull my hair!\nNow look at this cat, the cat is also pulling. \nWhat is the cat pulling? The cat is pulling its whiskers. Ouch! It hurts. This cat is pulling its whiskers out of boredom. The cat is so bored, I have nothing to do?\nWhat else can pull? The door. You can pull the door open, and push it back. Pull it open, push it back. Hey, don’t do that, you cannot play the door, don’t pull it too hard.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-038.jpg"},{"number":65,"word":"race","text":"3, 2, 1! Ready! Set! Go! What’s happening? Look, the animals are racing.\nRace, what does it mean? It means the animals are all running and they want to see who is the fastest. \nAnd who is the fastest? I’m curious.\nHere comes the panda. Hey panda, are you walking? You need to go faster.\nLet’s see who comes? The monkey is run really fast.\nHow about the deer? The deer is running really fast. The dog is super fast.\nHey, what was that? A car? What? Hey, that’s not fair! A car cannot join the race, because a car is super fast.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-035.jpg"},{"number":66,"word":"raise","text":"Raise your hand! Hi everyone, Susan wants to talk, so I’m raising my hand.\nNow look at this monkey, the monkey wants to talk too, so the monkey is raising its hand too. \nRaise your hand! Can you do it? Now raise your hand! Now let’s raise your hand slowly. Slowly raise your hand. Can you raise your hand really fast? Yes, I can!\nNow look at this, this is your hand, can you raise two hands? Yes, I can.\nCan you raise your feet? I can’t. Can you raise your feet? Yes. And can you raise you leg? Susan is raising my legs. What about your arms? I’m raising my arm.\nCan you raise your desk? I don’t think so, it’s too heavy.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-036.jpg"},{"number":67,"word":"refuse","text":"Hello dear darling, did your mommy say it to you this morning? Mommy says ‘hey baby, eat some carrots, it’s very good for you.’ ‘no, I refuse, it’s not yummy!’\n‘hey baby, eat some pees, it’s really yummy.’ ‘No! I refuse! It’s not yummy!’\n‘how about this baby? Try this apple.’ ’no! I refuse! It’s not yummy!’\n‘what? How about some candy? Do you want to eat some candy?’ ‘this I cannot refuse.’\nWhat does refuse mean? Refuse means ’ you say no! No! No! I don’t want it!’\nThe mouse refuses to drink water.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-033.jpg"},{"number":68,"word":"run","text":"Hello, look at these finger man, what’s my finger man doing? My finger man is running.\nSusan can run, can you run? Show me! That’s right, you can run very fast, right? \nBut I think I can run faster. What? You can run faster than me? Show me!  Wa~ you run so fast.\nLook at this lion, this lion is running so fast, can you run faster than the lion? Let’s try! \n3! 2! 1! Ready! Set! Go! Run! I think the lion runs faster.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-034.jpg"},{"number":69,"word":"scratch","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susans is scratching, because I feel so itchy, it’s itchy everywhere, I think I’ve got mosquito bites. Go away mosquitos, i’m so itchy, so I must scratch. so itchy!\nLook at these two badgers, this badger is scratching its friend’s back. \nWhy don’t we play the ‘super scratching’ game? 1, 2, 3, scratch your face! Scratch your ear! Scratch you neck! Scratch you shoulder! Scratch you head! Scratch your mommy!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-031.jpg"},{"number":70,"word":"salute \\ səˈluːt \\ 敬礼","text":"Hello, I am Susan, nice to meet you! Look at me, I am saluting, and this wolf is saluting another wolf. This wolf looks so cool, and this one is saluting! \n‘s-a-l-u-t-e’ makes \\ səˈluːt \\\nNow let’s do it! Salute! Salute! Scratch! Salute! Scratch! Oh, this is too fast. \nOk, one more time! Let’s salute again! Salute!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-032.jpg"},{"number":71,"word":"shake","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is shaking your hands. Shake my hand, oh, shake your little hand. \nLook at the two monkeys, the monkeys are shaking their hands after fighting. Oh, don’t fight, shake hands, let’s be friend. \nDo you know that famous song called ‘Hokey Pokey(变戏法)’? Let’s sing it together:\n‘you put your right hand in, you put your right hand out, \nYou put your right hand in and you shake it all about,\nYou do the hokey pokey, and you turn yourself around,\nThat's what it's all about.\n‘you put your (left) hand in, you put your (left) hand out, \nYou put your (left) hand in and you shake it all about,\nYou do the hokey pokey, and you turn yourself around,\nThat's what it's all about.’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-029.jpg"},{"number":72,"word":"shed \\ʃed\\落下","text":"Hey, everyone, why is Susan crying, Susan is feeling so sad, I am shedding tears, shed tears.\nWhy? Because I miss my baby and I miss my mom, I want to see them.\nNow look at this poor lion, the lion is shedding tears of sadness too. And why? Why are you shedding tears? ‘Roar, I’m hungry’, oh poor lion.\nHere comes grandma, grandma is shedding tears too. Why grandma? Why are you shedding tears? Because I miss your grandpa. Poor grandma.\nDad, why are you shedding tears? Because I’m so tired. What shall we do? why not give your dad a kiss!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-030.jpg"},{"number":73,"word":"show","text":"Today we’re gonna look at another word called ‘show’.\n‘sh’ makes \\ʃ\\.\nLook at this daddy monkey, the daddy monkey is showing its baby how to do a handstand. \nWhat? Handstand? Can you stand on you hand? I can’t, that’s really cool.\nCan you? I don’t know, maybe you can. \nWhat else can we show? Can you show me your eyes? Can you show me your ears? Can you show me your tongue? Hehe, that’s my tongue. \nCan you show your mommy that you love her? Yes, I love you mommy.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-027.jpg"},{"number":74,"word":"sing","text":"Do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti~~. What is Susan doing? Susan is practicing singing. \n‘ing’ makes \\ɪŋ\\\nI love singing, baby do you love singing? Today I will teach you how to sing ‘do re mi’ song\nDoe, a deer, a female deer. \nRay, a drop of golden sun.\nMe, a name I call myself.\nFar, a long, long way to run. \nSew, a needle pulling thread.\nLa, a note to follow sew.\nTea, a drink with jam and bread.\nThat will bring us back to do~~o~~o~~o. \nDo~re~mi~fa~so~la~ti~do~so~do!\nThe monkeys are joyfully singing.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-028.jpg"},{"number":75,"word":"slap","text":"What’s that? Look at the two lions, this lion is slapping another lion in the face. Oh no, that must be very painful, we cannot do that, do not slap anyone even you are really angry. \nWhat else can we slap? We can slap something on the table. What can we slap on the table? \nLook, the newspaper. Daddy, your newspaper. Hey baby, don’t slap the newspaper, it’s rude.\nWhat about this? Mommy, your envelope! Hey baby, don’t slap the envelope, it’s rude, you need to put it on the table.\nMy book! I slapped my book on the table. No baby, don’t slap you book, you need to love your book.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-025.jpg"},{"number":76,"word":"sleep","text":"Hi, sorry everyone, Susan was sleeping, because I am so sleepy.\nLook at the tiger, the tiger is sleeping on the branch. Don’t wake the tiger up.\nWhere does the monkey sleep? Maybe also on the branch, maybe the monkey can sleep on the branch too.\nHow about a panda, I think panda can sleep on the ground. Do you sleep on the ground? No, I want to sleep in my bed.\nHow about an owl? Wait a minute, an owl doesn’t sleep at night, an owl sleep in a day.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-026.jpg"},{"number":77,"word":"slither \\ˈslɪðə\\ 滑行","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is pretending to be a snake, and I am slithering. \nThis ‘th’ sounds very special, \\ð\\, can you say it? Very good!\nOh, the snake is slithering forward. Sometimes you can slither on the ice. be careful! Otherwise you will slip(本身有倒的意思).","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-023.jpg"},{"number":78,"word":"slurp \\lɜːrp\\ 啧啧，吸溜的声音","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is slurping the noodles, do you see the noodles? The noodles are very long and I don’t want to break them, so what do I do? Slurp them inside.\nYou can slurp the noodles and you can slurp the water. Look at this racoon, the raccoon is so cute. The racoon is happily slurping water through a straw.\nAnd you can slurp the noodles, you can slurp the juice, that’s so delicious. Can you slurp your noodles? Let’s slurp one more time. Funny!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-024.jpg"},{"number":79,"word":"smell","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is smelling. \nNow I want you to smell you mom, mommy smells like milk, do you think so?\nLook at this lion, this lion is smelling a beautiful flower, so fragrant(\\ˈfreɪɡrənt\\)!\nI like to smell flower, what about flowers? Let’s smell them. En~ fragrant!\nWhat about this? An apple smells so good, I want to eat it.\nWhat about somebody’s toot? Ew~so smelly!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-021.jpg"},{"number":80,"word":"smile","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is smiling. \ns-m-ai-l, don’t forget this \\l\\ sound.\nRemember we learned this one before? This is \\smel\\ and this one is \\smaɪ l\\\nI am so happy so I smile, now I’m gonna let some animals smile, and I want you to tell me who is smiling.\nWhich animal is smiling? That’s right, a dog is smiling.\nWhich animal? That’s right, it’s a cat, a cat is smiling.\nWhat’s that? It’s a tiger.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-022.jpg"},{"number":81,"word":"spit\\ spɪt\\","text":"Sorry, hi everyone, you’re right, I shouldn’t have done that. Because Susan just spat, spitting is bad.\nYou need to tell Susan, you say ‘Susan! No spitting!’ Very good! \nOne more time, ‘Susan! No spitting!’ That’s very good!\nLook at this word ‘spit’, oh no, don’t spit! Spitting is bad!\nLook at the tiger, the tiger is spitting, that’s really bad.\n‘sp’ makes \\sb\\ sound\nSometimes babies spit out, maybe because the baby is sick. And if you drink some bad milk, spit it out, it’s sour. but don’t spit out your medicine, because medicine will make you feel better.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-019.jpg"},{"number":82,"word":"spray","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is spraying myself with perfume. I love perfume, because it makes me smell really good. Does your mommy spray herself with perfume too? So your mom must smell very good.\nLook at this word, ‘spr’ is not read as \\spr\\, it’s read as \\sbr\\\nLook at the elephant, the elephant is spraying water.\nWhat’s that? It’s mosquito, now we need to get our insect spray. Ok we kill it.\nNow I want to go out to work, but I don’t like the color of my car, what should I do? I want to spray it blue!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-020.jpg"},{"number":83,"word":"stand","text":"‘hey Santa, where are you standing?’  ‘I’m standing on your shoulder.’ \n‘I don’t feel very comfortable when you stand there, can you get off?’  ‘Sure.’\n‘Ok Santa, where are you standing now?’ ‘I’m standing on you head.’\nHey everyone, this is a naughty Santa, and the Santa is standing on my head. I think you need to tell him to get off. \nCan you help me? You say ‘Santa, don’t stand on Susan!’ Alright, naughty Santa.\nLook, the hippo is standing in the water. Look at our Santa, it stands back on my shoulder.\nNow everyone, tell him not to stand there, you say ‘don’t’ stand on Susan’s shoulder!’ Thank you!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-017.jpg"},{"number":84,"word":"stare(接at)","text":"Hi everyone, what is susan doing? Susan is staring at you!\n‘st’ here makes \\sd\\ sound, it’s not \\s-t-er\\\nWhat does stare mean? Staring means you’re looking at something for a long time. Look this owl is staring at this man, they are staring at each other. \nAnd now I have got an orange, I want to stare at this orange wherever it goes. Can you stare at this orange with me?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-018.jpg"},{"number":85,"word":"stretch","text":"Hi good morning everyone, it’s an early start and Susan is stretching. I feel so good, did you stretch this morning? Look at this, we have a new word to look at. It’s stretch. \nAnd ‘str’ is not read as \\str\\, it’s \\sdr\\, so we have \\s-dr-e-tʃ\\, not \\s-tr-e-tʃ\\\nLook at the tiger, the tiger is stretching its body. \nNow let’s stretch. Look up! We stretch the front of our neck. Look down! We stretch the back of our neck.\nStretch again! Do you know that ant also stretch its own body in the morning?","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-015.jpg"},{"number":86,"word":"stroke \\strəʊk\\ 轻抚, 名词是‘一击’","text":"Hush little baby lion don’t say a word, mom’s gonna buy you a mockingbird知更鸟.’ Hush everybody, I am stroking the lion, I’m trying to put the baby lion to sleep. Ok and now, it’s sleeping there. \nI’m gonna teach you another word, it’s called stroke. \nYou stroke somebody to show that you love him or her. \nNow look at the monkeys, the father monkey is stroking its baby’s head with love. Oh, it’s so cute.\n‘str’ makes \\sdr\\ sound, don’t read it as \\s-tr-əʊ-k\\. No, no, no,it should be \\ sdrəʊk \\","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-016.jpg"},{"number":87,"word":"stuff","text":"Hello everybody, what is Susan doing? Susan is packing, I am stuffing, stuffing my bag with many things. \nNow look, jump rope! Because i need to do some exercise. \nUmbrella, i am stuffing my bag with my umbrella. \nAnd I’m gonna put the stickers inside, I’m gonna stuff my bag with the stickers. I’m gonna put the stickers everywhere in my home. \nAnd my water, i am stuffing my backpack. It’s so heavy~!\nThe squirrel is stuffing its mouth with food, and Susan stuffed my bag.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-013.jpg"},{"number":88,"word":"sulk \\sʌlk\\ 生闷气","text":"‘Hi Susan, what’s wrong with you? What are your doing?’   ‘En, I am sulking. ‘\n‘Why are you sulking?’  ‘Come on monkey, I am sulking, look, sulking’\n‘What does sulk mean?’   ‘Look, you sulk when you are really sad and angry and you don’t want to talk. I am sulking, I don’t want to talk at all!’ \n‘Susan, why are you sulking? Don’t’ sulk.’    ‘Oh monkey, thank you! Now I’m not sulking, because I’m happy now’ Look at this word, the monkey is sulking. You sulk when you feel angry and you don’t feel like talking. Maybe you wanna sulk in your own room.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-014.jpg"},{"number":89,"word":"swim","text":"Hi everyone, do you know what is Susan doing? Susan is swimming. \n‘sw’ makes \\sw\\ sound\nLook at this happy hippo, the hippo is swimming fast, swim really fast.\nWhat else can swim? Fish, a fish can swim really fast. And penguin, a penguin can swim super fast.\nWhat about your daddy? Oh no, may daddy cannot swim. Oh daddy, don’t jump in the pool! Help! Help!\nNow let’s go to save daddy! Swim!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-011.jpg"},{"number":90,"word":"teach","text":"Hi dear darling, today we’re gonna look at a new word, is called teach.\n‘ea’ makes the \\i:\\ sound, give me a big smile.\nLook at this leopard, this leopard is teaching geography. This is a map, so the teacher—the leopard teacher is pointing to the map and say ‘look, read after me’! \nHe is the teacher, he is teaching you.\nWho else is a teacher? Me! Susan is a teacher! I teach you English, I teach, you learn.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-012.jpg"},{"number":91,"word":"tease \\tiːz\\戏弄,嘲笑","text":"‘Hey susan, do you know what a monkey likes to eat?’   \n‘I know, I know, a monkey likes to eat watermelons. ‘\n‘hahaha, no,no, you are wrong, a monkey likes to eat bananas.’\n‘I know it, but why do I feel bad?’\n‘Hah, you are wrong! ’ \n‘Hey monkey, are you teasing me? Don’t tease me, you know teasing makes me feel bad.’\nLook monkey just now teased me. Don’t tease your friend, because if you tease your friend, they will feel so bad. Look at the fox, the fox is playfully teasing the racoon, so the racoon is not happy.\n‘Monkey, don’t tease me!’\n‘Ok, I’m sorry!’","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-009.jpg"},{"number":92,"word":"think","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is thinking. I am thinking of something.\n‘th’ makes a \\θ\\ sound. Don’t forget to put your tongue out.\nCan you guess what Susan is thinking? Susan is thinking of driving a car. \nNow what is Susan thinking now? Susan is thinking of eating a hamburger.\nWhat about now? Susan is thinking of drinking juice.\nThe owl is thinking of ideas.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-010.jpg"},{"number":93,"word":"waddle","text":"Hi everybody, what is susan doing? Susan is waddling like a penguin. A penguin can waddle. Oh no, there is not just one penguin, I see a line of penguins, they are all waddling. The penguins are waddling in a line.\nLeft, right, left, right. So a penguin can waddle. What else can waddle? A duck. Little ducks can waddle too.\nWhen some animal is fat with very short legs, they waddle. Now let’s waddle very slowly! Fast!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-007.jpg"},{"number":94,"word":"warm","text":"Hi everyone, Susan is so cold. Ok, I feel so cold, what should I do? You’re right, I should warm myself. \n‘w’ makes \\w\\ sound, it’s not \\wu\\, it’s \\wɔ\\\nLook at the lion, the lion is not cold, because the lion is warming itself by the fire. But Susan has no fire, I feel so cold, what should I do? You’re right, I should put on my jacket. \n‘put on your jacket, your jacket, your jacket.’ \nEn, I feel better, but my head is still a little cold. Yes, put on your hat. Put on your hat.\nSusan is so warm now.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-008.jpg"},{"number":95,"word":"warn","text":"Hi dear darling, today we are gonna look at a very cool word, it’s called warn.\nLook at the lion, what is the lion saying? The lion is warning the vulture to stay away. \nThe lion is saying ‘that’s my meat, I warn you, don’t eat it! Go away!’ The lion is warning the vulture.\n‘w’ for \\w\\\nI warn you, you know your mom will warn you against possible dangerous. \nFor example, oh no, bayb don’t touch it, it’s too hot, you may hurt you fingers.\nOh, no, no, no, baby hold my hand, we are crossing the street, the car is coming, it’s dangerous.\nOh no, no, no, baby, don’t touch that, it’s a knife!","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-005.jpg"},{"number":96,"word":"wash","text":"1, 2, 3, 4, oh hello everybody, what is Susan doing? Susan is washing her face.\n‘sh’ makes ‘\\ʃ\\’ sound.\nOh, look at the lion, the lion is washing its face. Why don’t we wash our face?\nNow what’s this? You’re right, it’s my hair. Oh, my hair is a little dirty, what shall we do? Wash your hair.\nAnd my hands are so dirty, what shall we do? You’re right, wash your hands. Now look, my hands are so clean.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-006.jpg"},{"number":97,"word":"weigh \\weɪ\\ 称重","text":"Oh my god, my bag is so heavy, I wanna know how heavy it is. Let’s weigh it, put it on the scale. Oh my, it’s so heavy.\nYou know what? We can use a scale to weigh things. A scale can tell you how heavy something is.\nWhat’s this? It’s a rhino, the rhino is weighing itself on the scale. Let’s weigh the cow. The cow is so heavy!\nWhat about the owl? The owl is so light. Now let’s weigh the baby, the baby is so light.\nDaddy, your turn to go on the scale. No, I don’t want, I’m too fat. Daddy, you got to lose some weight.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-003.jpg"},{"number":98,"word":"whistle.","text":"Hey everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is whistling\n‘wh’ makes w\\ sound. And this ‘l' makes \\l\\ sound So together, lets read it one more time!\nLook at the horse, the horse is so happy and the horse is happily whistling.\nWhen do you need to whistle? You whistle when you want to call your doggy back. Let’s whistle, oh\nlittle puppy, come, come.\nAnd then sometimes, you whistle to call your horse back. And the horse is coming back. That’s right","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-004.jpg"},{"number":99,"word":"wiggle","text":"Hello everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is wiggling her hair.\nLook at the lion, the lion has a long tail, and the lion is wiggling its tail.\nHere ‘gg’ makes \\g\\ sound.\nWhich other animal can wiggle? A puppy! A puppy has a long tail too, and it will wiggle its tail to say ‘I’m so happy’.\nOk, let’s wiggle our finger, wiggle your thumbkin, wiggle your pointer, wiggle your nose, and you can wiggle your ears.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-001.jpg"},{"number":100,"word":"yawn \\jɔːn\\","text":"Hi everyone, what is Susan doing? Susan is yawning. Why? Why is Susan yawning? Because Susan is so sleepy.\nOh, look at the monkey, the monkey is yawning sleepily, the monkey wants to sleep too.\nHey Susan, why are you yawning in the morning? Because I didn’t get enough sleep last night.\nHey Susan, why are you yawning after lunch? cause I eat too much and I feel like sleeping.\nHey Susan, why are you yawning now? Because it’s bed time.","image":"assets/verb-cards/card-002.jpg"}];
